WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.970 line:0
Begin with parent atoms in an ideal closed system.

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:09.520 line:0
During the first half-life, parents decay until fifty percent

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:09.760 line:0
remain.

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:17.200 line:0
During the second half-life, the parent fraction falls to

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.940 line:0
twenty-five percent, leaving seventy-five percent daughters.

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:25.240 line:0
During the third half-life, the parent fraction falls to

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:29.100 line:0
twelve and a half percent. Equal intervals remove half

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:29.740 line:0
of what remains.

00:00:30.737 --> 00:00:33.717 line:0
Dating requires checking the initial composition and whether the

00:00:33.717 --> 00:00:34.697 line:0
system stayed closed.
